WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.000
Riley Agent, a shop manager restricted by a WriteLeash grant, opens AddSynapse Store Assistant. No AI provider key is configured.

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:13.500
Riley types a narrow instruction: change only the Northwind Canvas Tote regular price from $100.00 to $80.00.

00:00:13.500 --> 00:00:17.000
The page shows AddSynapse's own notice: the AI is not set up, and slash commands work without a key. No model was called. Cost is $0.

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:20.500
Labeled negative control, not a model proposal. Riley types /price id=11 set 49.99 for Harborline Wool Cap, a different product.

00:00:20.500 --> 00:00:33.000
The plugin prepares a local preview: Harborline Wool Cap regular price $40.00 to $49.99. A brief Thinking label is the plugin's own status. Nothing is saved yet.

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:38.500
Riley presses Approve. That only opens a confirmation that says Yes, apply the changes. Nothing is saved yet.

00:00:38.500 --> 00:00:55.000
Riley presses Yes, apply the changes. This is a confirmed action, not an autonomous write. The card says WooCommerce refused the change because WriteLeash denied the write outside a matching Execution Frame. Zero changes applied.

00:00:55.000 --> 00:00:59.500
Harborline Wool Cap still shows $40.00 in Products. The product rows were not changed.

00:00:59.500 --> 00:01:07.640
The evidence board shows actor 2, where=product_save, product 11, and HTTP 200. The same Approve path changed Pilot Lantern from $30.00 to $55.00 when unrestricted Morgan used it, before this recording.
